      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>POTENTIAL CONFLICTS OF INTEREST ARE REVIEWED AND DETERMINED AT THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS LEVEL. ALL DIRECTORS ARE REQUESTED TO DISCLOSE ANY POTENTIAL OR CURRENT CONFLICTS OF INTEREST. IF A CONFLICT ARISES, THE PERSON WITH THE CONFLICT IS NOT ALLOWED TO VOTE ON THE TRANSACTION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION'S EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE REVIEWS AND APPROVES THE COMPENSATION FOR THE ORGANIZATION'S CEO AND OTHER OFFICERS. THE PROCESS FOR DETERMINING AND ESTABLISHING COMPENSATION INCLUDES USE OF DATA SUCH AS REVIEW OF MARKET PAY RATES FOR COMPARABLE COMPENSATION INFORMATION FOR SIMILARLY QUALIFIED PERSONS IN FUNCTIONALLY COMPARABLE POSITIONS AT SIMILARLY SITUATED ORGANIZATIONS. PERSONS WITH A CONFLICT OF INTEREST REGARDING THE COMPENSATION ARRANGEMENT AT ISSUE ARE NOT INVOLVED. THE ORGANIZATION MAINTAINS CONTEMPORANEOUS DOCUMENTATION AND RECORDKEEPING FOR DELIBERATIONS AND DECISIONS REGARDING THE COMPENSATION ARRANGEMENT. THIS PROCESS WAS LAST DONE AND DOCUMENTED IN DECEMBER 2024. THE ORGANIZATION DOES NOT HAVE ANY KEY EMPLOYEES.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
